Source: tekne-nvidia
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tekne project <noreply@tekne.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tekne-nvidia
Architecture: all
# The driver comes from NVIDIA's repository (tekne-nvidia-repo, DEC-041):
# open kernel modules only, for Turing and newer GPUs. Devuan's own 550 is
# older than 615 and doesn't build for Tekne's kernel, so it can't satisfy
# these. The kernel headers come from excalibur-backports (DEC-036) for DKMS.
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 tekne-nvidia-repo,
 nvidia-driver (>= 615),
 nvidia-kernel-open-dkms (>= 615),
 linux-headers-amd64
Description: NVIDIA's display driver, set up for Tekne (opt-in)
 Installs NVIDIA's current display driver from NVIDIA's repository (through
 tekne-nvidia-repo) and sets it up for Tekne's hybrid-graphics laptops:
 the desktop stays on the integrated GPU, the NVIDIA GPU powers off when
 idle, and tekne-prime-run runs a program on it (PRIME render offload).
 Suspend and hibernate use the driver's kernel notifiers, with no systemd.
 .
 Open kernel modules only: Turing (GTX 16xx, RTX 20xx) and newer GPUs.
 Purge it, and the driver's packages, to go back to nouveau.
